      "fontSize": 10,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Comprehension Protocol (comprehension-protocol.md)\n\nRule: memory encodes understanding; never encode confusion. All 5 gates open before encode.\nGate 1 LOCATE: field/subfield · neighbors · special/general · problem solved · 1-min map 2 sentences · anti-pattern: read before category.\nGate 2 REPRESENT: ≥3 distinct forms from {verbal · symbolic · geometric · computational · adversarial · extreme} — min 3 of 6.\nGate 3 MINIMIZE: smallest example still exhibiting phenomenon (Tao/Feynman move).\nGate 4 FALSIFY: what would break · edge cases · null experiments.\nGate 5 REGENERATE: derive from scratch without notes — only real test.\nLive lectures: thin pass Locate+Represent skeleton+tags; Gate 5 soon after class before heavy encoding → lecture-listening-notes.md.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Comprehension Protocol (comprehension-protocol.md)\n\nRule: memory encodes understanding; never encode confusion. All 5 gates open before encode.\nGate 1 LOCATE: field/subfield · neighbors · special/general · problem solved · 1-min map 2 sentences · anti-pattern: read before category.\nGate 2 REPRESENT: ≥3 distinct forms from {verbal · symbolic · geometric · computational · adversarial · extreme} — min 3 of 6.\nGate 3 MINIMIZE: smallest example still exhibiting phenomenon (Tao/Feynman move).\nGate 4 FALSIFY: what would break · edge cases · null experiments.\nGate 5 REGENERATE: derive from scratch without notes — only real test.\nLive lectures: thin pass Locate+Represent skeleton+tags; Gate 5 soon after class before heavy encoding → lecture-listening-notes.md.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 9
    },
